# Working directory for card description generation
output/*
# Everything under output/ is bulk intermediate data and stays ignored - but the audit's
# evidence record is hand-written and cannot be regenerated, so it is versioned. Without this
# the whole remediation's proof trail would exist on exactly one machine.
!output/remediation/
output/remediation/*
!output/remediation/AUDIT_LOG.md
# The list of what only Martin can decide (2026-09-21). It is addressed to him, it is not derivable
# from any run, and a file directly under `output/remediation/` is silently swallowed by the glob
# above - which is how a deliverable goes missing without a word.
!output/remediation/HUMAN_ONLY.md
# The old-to-new commit table for the 2026-09-21 history rewrite. It cannot be regenerated -
# filter-branch does not keep its mapping - and every hash recorded before the rewrite is
# stale without it, so it is versioned like AUDIT_LOG.md rather than left to the glob.
!output/remediation/HISTORY_REWRITE_*.md
# The instruments this remediation was actually run with (2026-09-22): the 100-step write gate, its
# independent acceptance, the plan builder, the hold list and the census scripts. 1,577 lines of
# Python, the only implementation of the write path - rehearsed against production, journalled,
# reversible - and without them a fresh clone can neither repeat nor check a single one of the 994
# writes. Same reason as AUDIT_LOG.md: a proof trail must not live on one machine.
!output/remediation/tools/
# Two hand-written reports from the first day of the audit that nothing can regenerate, plus the
# entry point written for whoever picks this up next.
!output/remediation/BETWEEN_REPORT.md
!output/remediation/CENSUS.md
!output/remediation/HANDOVER.md
# The gold standard is web research: 36 sites judged field by field against live sources. Nothing in
# the repo can regenerate it, so it is versioned for the same reason as the log - and its
# comparison script with it, so the false-negative rate is recomputable rather than asserted.
!output/remediation/gold_standard/
# The per-site verdict records behind that report are the primary evidence for every number in it.
# Small in total (~300 KB) and equally irreproducible; the bulk caches next to them stay ignored.
# Each intermediate directory has to be re-included in turn: git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so negating a file two levels down silently does nothing.
!output/remediation/gold_scratch/
output/remediation/gold_scratch/*
!output/remediation/gold_scratch/records/

# Dev artifacts
*.stackdump
test*.jpg
card-mockup.html


# Site-shorts / paper-video working assets (local renders, never served)
video-assets/

# Vitest cache (created by vitest run)
.vitest/

# Hero repair (Phase 2 step 1): bulk regenerable artifacts. `apply.py --emit` reproduces APPLY.sql
# byte-identically (sha256 33cbab582f830378, re-proved after the formatter) and `plan.py --write`
# reproduces PLAN.jsonl; the applied statement's effect is in the database and in
# remediation_change_log. ROLLBACK.sql IS versioned even though it regenerates too, because it
# describes an action not yet taken - the undo. APPLIED.md is the evidence record.
# The directory must be re-included first: git does not descend into an excluded directory.
!output/remediation/hero_repair/
output/remediation/hero_repair/APPLY.sql
output/remediation/hero_repair/REHEARSAL.sql
output/remediation/hero_repair/PLAN.jsonl

# --- Remediation deliverables -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Rule (established 2026-09-21): version what cannot be regenerated - designs, briefs, measurement
# records, generators, and the undo. Ignore bulk that a generator rebuilds on demand. A directory
# negation must come BEFORE its file-level rules; git does not descend into an excluded directory.
!output/remediation/gallery_design/
!output/remediation/phase3_worklist/
output/remediation/phase3_worklist/WORKLIST.jsonl

!output/remediation/phase3_runner/
# Plans are regenerable and are therefore not versioned - the rule at the top of this block. The
# snapshot plan over all 5,004 sites was regenerated on 2026-09-21 and came back with the identical
# sha256 (a5786f102c8352bbfe94eb9ecfd9dc7d0b8b15625f4ac94b6753a245572716bb), which is the proof that
# it is derivable; the hash itself is recorded in AUDIT_LOG.md and PIECE7.md, where it cannot rot.
# 12 MB of generated JSON in the history would be paid for by every clone, forever.
output/remediation/phase3_runner/PLAN*.jsonl
output/remediation/phase3_runner/runs/
# The append lock is machine state, not data: `Ledger.append` holds it only while it writes a line,
# and the operating system frees it when a writer dies. It must never be versioned or deleted.
output/remediation/phase3_runner/LEDGER.jsonl.lock
# The Phase-4 runner (2026-09-24), versioned by the same rule: the pilot's sealed artefacts
# (PILOT.jsonl, gold_prose_errors.json, PILOT_THRESHOLDS.md), the small reads they were drawn from
# (S0_ROUTELESS.json, S0_ITEM_NAMES.json) and the ledgers are the record. The production export
# (S0_ROWS.jsonl: every curated description and raw_data, ~20 MB) and the plans built from it are
# bulk that `plan4.py read`/`build` rebuild from a fresh read; their sha256 are in AUDIT_LOG.md. The
# runs hold Wikipedia text and the repository is public (design, source_store: RETENTION), so they
# stay on the workstation with the names lookup's evidence.
!output/remediation/phase4_runner/
output/remediation/phase4_runner/S0_ROWS.jsonl
output/remediation/phase4_runner/PLAN*.jsonl
# Lane L's own read and plan (2026-09-25): the same bulk, rebuilt by `plan4.py read`/`legacy`.
output/remediation/phase4_runner/LEGACY4*.jsonl
output/remediation/phase4_runner/runs/
output/remediation/phase4_runner/plan_evidence/
output/remediation/phase4_runner/LEDGER*.jsonl.lock
!output/remediation/mechanical/
# APPLY.sql and PLAN.jsonl are pinned rather than ignored: the deploy lens established that
# the generator cannot reproduce them, and APPLY.sql is the exact statement set that wrote
# the 35-row country change, whose journal rows are already in production. Versioning the
# undo while ignoring the apply is half an audit trail. REHEARSAL.sql stays out: it rolls
# back inside its own transaction and writes nothing.
output/remediation/mechanical/REHEARSAL.sql
# The later mechanical lanes (2026-09-22) are versioned the same way: the plan, the refusals, the
# undo and, once emitted, the statement - never the rehearsal, which rolls itself back.
!output/remediation/mechanical_uk/
output/remediation/mechanical_uk/REHEARSAL.sql
!output/remediation/mechanical_period_name/
output/remediation/mechanical_period_name/REHEARSAL.sql
!output/remediation/mechanical_site_type/
output/remediation/mechanical_site_type/REHEARSAL.sql
# The cell lanes (2026-09-23): versioned the same way. A card_stats wave follows the hero repair's
# rule instead: its production export (every curated description, ~7 MB), PLAN.jsonl (~8 MB) and
# APPLY.sql (~5 MB) are bulk that `card_stats.py --export/--write` and `apply.py --emit` rebuild;
# PLAN.md, SKIPPED.jsonl, the undo (ROLLBACK.sql) and the basis the next wave's proof reads
# (BASIS.json, ~0.4 MB) are versioned. A wave is re-planned from a fresh export right before it is
# applied, so the versioned undo and basis are the applied plan's only then.
# The scope lane's fetched pages are bulk and regenerable (`scope.py --collect`).
!output/remediation/mechanical_card_stats/
output/remediation/mechanical_card_stats/*/export/
output/remediation/mechanical_card_stats/*/PLAN.jsonl
output/remediation/mechanical_card_stats/*/APPLY.sql
output/remediation/mechanical_card_stats/*/REHEARSAL.sql
!output/remediation/mechanical_scope/
output/remediation/mechanical_scope/export/
output/remediation/mechanical_scope/REHEARSAL.sql
!output/remediation/mechanical_reversal_1/
output/remediation/mechanical_reversal_1/REHEARSAL.sql
!output/remediation/mechanical_reversal_2/
output/remediation/mechanical_reversal_2/REHEARSAL.sql
!output/remediation/mechanical_reversal_3/
output/remediation/mechanical_reversal_3/REHEARSAL.sql
!output/remediation/mechanical_wrong_both/
output/remediation/mechanical_wrong_both/REHEARSAL.sql
# The site_external_ids repair (2026-09-22): hand-researched, not regenerable from any run, and not yet
# applied - the plan, the statement, the undo and the evidence are versioned; the rehearsal keeps
# nothing and is rendered again by `qid_repair.py render`.
!output/remediation/qid_repair/
output/remediation/qid_repair/REHEARSAL.sql
output/remediation/qid_repair/wave2/REHEARSAL.sql
output/remediation/qid_repair/wave3/REHEARSAL.sql
output/remediation/qid_repair/wave4/REHEARSAL.sql
# The owner cases of HUMAN_ONLY section B (2026-09-23): the per-site verdicts with their evidence, the
# duplicate list the scope lane reads, the research behind the external-id repair's second wave and the
# coordinate plan. Rendered from Wikidata and Wikipedia answers of one day, so not regenerable byte for
# byte later - versioned like the qid_repair plan. The production export and the HTTP answers
# (`cache/bcases/`) stay out; the rehearsal keeps nothing.
!output/remediation/bcases/
output/remediation/bcases/coords_plan/REHEARSAL.sql
output/remediation/bcases/coords_plan_wave2/REHEARSAL.sql
# The gap run's decision record is versioned; its production export is bulk and regenerable
# (`gap_plan.py export`), and PLAN.gap.jsonl is covered by the phase3_runner PLAN*.jsonl rule.
!output/remediation/gap/
output/remediation/gap/export/
output/remediation/gap/scratch/
!output/remediation/phase3_pilot/

# Raw third-party response bodies, fetched as evidence during the Phase-3 pilot, are NOT versioned.
# gitleaks reported seven live third-party credentials inside verbatim public HTML in this directory
# (Google/Mapbox/Carto client keys published by the sites themselves) - keys we cannot rotate because
# they are not ours, so .gitleaksignore must not exempt them. The rule above is placed BEFORE this one
# on purpose: a directory negation has to precede the rules that re-exclude paths beneath it.
# What survives as the record: fetch_log.jsonl keeps url, http status, byte count and sha256 per fetch,
# and the extracted evidence text already lives in PILOT.jsonl. The bodies stay on the workstation.
output/remediation/phase3_pilot/evidence/

# G0: the verdict persister. All of it is versioned, including APPLY.sql and PLAN.jsonl: the
# premise that they are "regenerable" was false. They are rendered from
# `video-assets/shorts/*/selection.json`, which is gitignored working data that never leaves the
# workstation, so on any other checkout the same command reproduces nothing - and the write they
# describe is already in `remediation_change_log` (run_stamp 2026-09-21_gallery-verdicts-persist,
# 105 rows). The plan and the two scripts are the record and the undo of that write, not a cache.
!output/remediation/gallery_audit/
# S1 liveness stores: COMMONS.jsonl holds one line per referenced Commons file (46,070 lines, about
# 30 MB) and stays on the workstation; SUMMARY.json pins its sha256, and NOT_LIVE.jsonl - the lines
# every L1/L2 write cites - is versioned with the plan. The vision ledgers of the G runs
# (run-*/VERDICTS.jsonl, raw responses, 150-250 MB for a full run) are archived by the HANDOVER
# section 3 rule, not versioned. The C1 ledger is: calibration-*/VERDICTS.jsonl (about 940 lines,
# about 4 MB at the pilot's 4 kB per line) is what `calibrate.verify_admission` re-derives
# ADMISSION.json from before any vision write, so its exact bytes are versioned with the seal.
output/remediation/gallery_audit/liveness-*/COMMONS.jsonl
output/remediation/gallery_audit/run-*/VERDICTS.jsonl

# VLM competence pilot. The measurement and its generators are versioned: VLM.jsonl cost 200
# billed vision calls and cannot be regenerated identically, and the scripts are the method.
# The 24 MB of contact sheets and 4.6 MB of tile crops are rebuilt on demand by make_sheets.py,
# so they stay out. As always the negation comes BEFORE the rules that re-exclude beneath it.
!output/remediation/vlm_pilot/
output/remediation/vlm_pilot/tiles/
output/remediation/vlm_pilot/contact_sheet_*.png
output/remediation/vlm_pilot/__pycache__/
output/remediation/vlm_pilot/*.log
output/remediation/vlm_pilot/*.partial.jsonl
# The Opus re-verification of every DeepSeek-decided production row (2026-09-23): its sealed rules,
# its input and every verdict are the proof behind any reversal it leads to.
!output/remediation/opus_audit/
# The third-party pages the quote check fetched (raw bytes, PDFs among them) stay local; PAGES.jsonl
# records each one's status and the sha256 of its bytes.
output/remediation/opus_audit/pages/
# The Phase-6 acceptance (2026-09-25): its sealed protocol, the draw script's exclusion id lists
# and - once taken, after the last write - the draw. CANARIES.jsonl stays local until the scoring:
# it is the answer key of the canary questions, and DRAW.json pins its sha256 when it is written.
!output/remediation/acceptance/
output/remediation/acceptance/draw-*/CANARIES.jsonl
# The judging of a draw (scripts/remediation/acceptance/judge.py) keeps its files in judging/: the
# questions there carry the planted canary values, and beside the committed SAMPLE.jsonl they give
# the key away. They stay local until RESULT.json is written and are committed with it and with
# CANARIES.jsonl (`git add -f` on judging/*.jsonl and judging/*.json); the fetched pages' raw bytes
# (judging/pages/) stay local for good - PAGES.jsonl records each one's sha256.
output/remediation/acceptance/draw-*/judging/
# The name-key lane (Phase 6 item 2): its production read and chunks, versioned like the image
# lanes' (the chunk's ROLLBACK.sql is the undo of a write).
!output/remediation/name_key/
# The sitelink pilot's question list is one of the acceptance draw's fixed exclusion sources
# (scripts/remediation/acceptance/draw.py FIXED_EXCLUSIONS, pinned in EXCLUSIONS.sha256.json):
# the draw reads it and tests/remediation/test_acceptance_draw.py checks its sha256, so it must
# exist on every checkout, CI included (a clean checkout failed that test on 2026-09-25). The
# rest of the sitelink directories (plans, production exports, fetched sitelinks) stays local.
!output/remediation/sitelink/
output/remediation/sitelink/*
!output/remediation/sitelink/pilot/
output/remediation/sitelink/pilot/*
!output/remediation/sitelink/pilot/questions.json
